data: {"result":{"content":[{"type":"text","text":"## Validated recipe — uniswap-v3@70bc2e40\n\n⚠ Version disagreement: this recipe was validated against `uniswap-v3@70bc2e40`, while the units below are labelled `uniswap-v3@3.0.0`. Both are stated rather than reconciled — a recipe's stamp records what was actually run, and a unit's label records what the corpus holds. Differences inside one major are not always cosmetic: check the recipe's own pins before copying it against these units.\n_human-validated 2026-08-11 by farseen (github: FarseenSh)_\n_source: recipes/uniswap-v3/exact-input-swap.yaml_\n\n**Receipts** — what was actually run, on 2026-08-11, by farseen (github: FarseenSh)\n- checks: attest, test, fork\n- chains exercised: ethereum, base, arbitrum\n- on-chain:\n  - none recorded — this row exercises no chain, or its run broadcast nothing. A stated absence, never a gap: the receipt for such a row IS the suite result.\n- gas: see `gas_notes` — the measured figures live there with their conditions, and a receipt that restated them without those conditions would be a number without its composition.\n\n# Recipe: uniswap-v3 @3 :: exact-input-swap\n# STATUS: ✅ VALIDATED 2026-08-11 by farseen (github: FarseenSh) — 7 quotes · 9 structural · 7 fork assertions, and THE FLOW RAN ON ALL THREE CHAINS. (Banner and stamp changed in the SAME edit — see aave-v3, where this drifted twice.)\nproject_id: \"uniswap-v3\"    # ⚠ The locked P1 worklist brands the major into the id. §2 rules\n                            #   those ids are NOT renamed, and version_major is set redundantly.\nversion_major: 3            # the protocol major — and here it agrees with the id, unlike `dynamic`\nversion: \"70bc2e40\"         # ⚠ NOT a semver. SwapRouter02 publishes no version; this is the\n                            #   pinned commit's short SHA, the only version identity it has.\ntype: \"exact-input-swap\"\n\n# Every one of these had the FLOW run on it, not just the deployment inspected.\nchains: [ethereum, base, arbitrum]\n\n# ── THE DEPLOYMENTS ─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────\n# ⚠ SwapRouter02 is NOT at one address across chains. Verified on-chain by selector, not copied.#\n# ⚠ NAMED 2026-08-15 (F-4, protocol rule 9). Each chain previously mapped straight to a bare\n#   address, so the typed table produced a row with no contract name — \"(unnamed in recipe)\" —\n#   and the address could be served but not asked for. The name is NOT the author's: it is the\n#   contract name Sourcify reports for the verified source at that exact address on that exact\n#   chain, attested in sources.json. ⚠ NO ADDRESS CHANGED; only a name was added around it.\n# 🔴 THIS EDIT POSTDATES THE STAMP ABOVE and the stamp was not touched — this row needs a fresh\n#   curator run before launch. Every address here resolves to `SwapRouter02` on every chain listed.\ndeployments:\n  ethereum:\n    SwapRouter02: \"0x68b3465833fb72A70ecDF485E0e4C7bD8665Fc45\"\n  arbitrum:\n    SwapRouter02: \"0x68b3465833fb72A70ecDF485E0e4C7bD8665Fc45\"\n  base:\n    SwapRouter02: \"0x2626664c2603336E57B271c5C0b26F421741e481\"\n\n# ── WORKING EXAMPLE ─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────\n# Extracted VERBATIM to test/uniswap-v3/recipe/ and COMPILED BY FOUNDRY there, so \"the shipped\n# example is broken\" is a build failure rather than a discovery (recipe #1, D-1).\nworking_example:\n  source_protocol: \"uniswap-v3\"\n  source_url: \"https://github.com/Uniswap/swap-router-contracts/blob/70bc2e40dfca294c1cea9bf67a4036732ee54303/contracts/interfaces/IV3SwapRouter.sol\"\n  code: |\n    // ── WorkingExample.sol ──\n    // SPDX-License-Identifier: MIT\n    pragma solidity ^0.8.24;\n\n    interface IERC20 {\n        function approve(address spender, uint256 amount) external returns (bool);\n        function transferFrom(address from, address to, uint256 amount) external returns (bool);\n    }\n\n    /// SwapRouter02's V3 surface. SEVEN fields — there is no `deadline` here.\n    interface IV3SwapRouter {\n        struct ExactInputSingleParams {\n            address tokenIn;\n            address tokenOut;\n            uint24 fee;\n            address recipient;\n            uint256 amountIn;\n            uint256 amountOutMinimum;\n            uint160 sqrtPriceLimitX96;\n        }\n\n        function exactInputSingle(ExactInputSingleParams calldata params)\n            external\n            payable\n            returns (uint256 amountOut);\n    }\n\n    /// Where the deadline actually lives on SwapRouter02.\n    interface IMulticallExtended {\n        function multicall(uint256 deadline, bytes[] calldata data)\n            external\n            payable\n            returns (bytes[] memory results);\n    }\n\n    contract ExactInputSwapper {\n        address public immutable router;\n\n        /// ⚠ The router address is a CONSTRUCTOR ARGUMENT, deliberately. SwapRouter02 is at\n        ///   0x68b3465833fb72A70ecDF485E0e4C7bD8665Fc45 on Ethereum and Arbitrum but\n        ///   0x2626664c2603336E57B271c5C0b26F421741e481 on Base, so a hard-coded constant is a\n        ///   bug waiting for a deployment. See common_mistakes #3.\n        constructor(address router_) {\n            router = router_;\n        }\n\n        /// Swap an exact amount of tokenIn for as much tokenOut as possible.\n        ///\n        /// ⚠ THE DEADLINE IS NOT IN THE PARAMS. It is supplied by wrapping the call in\n        ///   multicall(deadline, …). Calling exactInputSingle directly compiles, runs, and has\n        ///   NO deadline protection whatsoever. See common_mistakes #2.\n        function swapExactInputSingle(\n            address tokenIn,\n            address tokenOut,\n            uint24 fee,\n            uint256 amountIn,\n            uint256 amountOutMinimum,\n            uint256 deadline\n        ) external returns (uint256 amountOut) {\n            IERC20(tokenIn).transferFrom(msg.sender, address(this), amountIn);\n            IERC20(tokenIn).approve(router, amountIn);\n\n            IV3SwapRouter.ExactInputSingleParams memory params = IV3SwapRouter.ExactInputSingleParams({\n                tokenIn: tokenIn,\n                tokenOut: tokenOut,\n                fee: fee,\n                recipient: msg.sender,\n                // ⚠ NEVER pass 0 here expecting a no-op. On SwapRouter02, 0 means \"swap the\n                //   router's entire balance of tokenIn\". See common_mistakes #4.\n                amountIn: amountIn,\n                amountOutMinimum: amountOutMinimum,\n                sqrtPriceLimitX96: 0\n            });\n\n            bytes[] memory calls = new bytes[](1);\n            calls[0] = abi.encodeCall(IV3SwapRouter.exactInputSingle, (params));\n\n            bytes[] memory results = IMulticallExtended(router).multicall(deadline, calls);\n\n_… recipe truncated for budget — 34282 bytes total, full text at the source path above._\n_Continue it: `web3_fetch` with `cursor: \"recipe:uniswap-v3@70bc2e40::exact-input-swap::body@5600\"` — each call returns the next slice and the next cursor until there is none._\n\n**Citations** (preserved through truncation — degrade bodies, never citations):\n- https://github.com/Uniswap/swap-router-contracts/blob/70bc2e40dfca294c1cea9bf67a4036732ee54303/contracts/interfaces/IV3SwapRouter.sol\n- https://github.com/Uniswap/v3-periphery/blob/0682387198a24c7cd63566a2c58398533860a5d1/contracts/interfaces/ISwapRouter.sol\n- https://github.com/Uniswap/swap-router-contracts/blob/70bc2e40dfca294c1cea9bf67a4036732ee54303/contracts/interfaces/IMulticallExtended.sol\n- https://github.com/Uniswap/universal-router\n- https://github.com/Uniswap/swap-router-contracts\n- https://raw.githubusercontent.com/Uniswap/swap-router-contracts/70bc2e40dfca294c1cea9bf67a4036732ee54303/contracts/interfaces/IV3SwapRouter.sol\n- https://github.com/Uniswap/swap-router-contracts/tree/70bc2e40dfca294c1cea9bf67a4036732ee54303\n- https://github.com/Uniswap/v3-periphery/tree/0682387198a24c7cd63566a2c58398533860a5d1\n\n---\n\n### uniswap-v3@3.0.0::UniswapSwapper::__contract__\n`uniswap-v3@3.0.0` · ⚠ version_defaulted · repo:d0831dc6b8a318df3872b6d68f6de135c9f3ec29 · as_of 2026-04-30T16:18:48Z\nhttps://github.com/Uniswap/v3-core/blob/d0831dc6b8a318df3872b6d68f6de135c9f3ec29/audits/tob/contracts/crytic/echidna/Setup.sol#L151-L205\n\n```\ncontract UniswapSwapper {\n    UniswapV3Pool pool;\n```\n\n### uniswap-v3@3.0.0::E2E_swap::test_swap_exactOut_zeroForOne\n`uniswap-v3@3.0.0` · ⚠ version_defaulted · repo:d0831dc6b8a318df3872b6d68f6de135c9f3ec29 · as_of 2026-04-30T16:18:48Z\nhttps://github.com/Uniswap/v3-core/blob/d0831dc6b8a318df3872b6d68f6de135c9f3ec29/audits/tob/contracts/crytic/echidna/E2E_swap.sol#L420-L452\n\n```\nfunction test_swap_exactOut_zeroForOne(uint128 _amount) public {\n        require(_amount != 0);\n```\n\n### uniswap-v3@3.0.0::E2E_swap::test_swap_exactOut_oneForZero\n`uniswap-v3@3.0.0` · ⚠ version_defaulted · repo:d0831dc6b8a318df3872b6d68f6de135c9f3ec29 · as_of 2026-04-30T16:18:48Z\nhttps://github.com/Uniswap/v3-core/blob/d0831dc6b8a318df3872b6d68f6de135c9f3ec29/audits/tob/contracts/crytic/echidna/E2E_swap.sol#L454-L486\n\n```\nfunction test_swap_exactOut_oneForZero(uint128 _amount) public {\n        require(_amount != 0);\n```\n\n### uniswap-v3@3.0.0::test.shared.utilities::createMultiPoolFunctions\n`uniswap-v3@3.0.0` · ⚠ version_defaulted · repo:d0831dc6b8a318df3872b6d68f6de135c9f3ec29 · as_of 2026-04-30T16:18:48Z\nhttps://github.com/Uniswap/v3-core/blob/d0831dc6b8a318df3872b6d68f6de135c9f3ec29/test/shared/utilities.ts#L229-L258\n\n```\nexport function createMultiPoolFunctions({\n  inputToken,\n```\n\n### uniswap-v3@3.0.0::E2E_swap::test_swap_exactIn_zeroForOne\n`uniswap-v3@3.0.0` · ⚠ version_defaulted · repo:d0831dc6b8a318df3872b6d68f6de135c9f3ec29 · as_of 2026-04-30T16:18:48Z\nhttps://github.com/Uniswap/v3-core/blob/d0831dc6b8a318df3872b6d68f6de135c9f3ec29/audits/tob/contracts/crytic/echidna/E2E_swap.sol#L352-L384\n\n```\nfunction test_swap_exactIn_zeroForOne(uint128 _amount) public {\n        require(_amount != 0);\n```\n\n### uniswap-v3@3.0.0::E2E_swap::test_swap_exactIn_oneForZero\n`uniswap-v3@3.0.0` · ⚠ version_defaulted · repo:d0831dc6b8a318df3872b6d68f6de135c9f3ec29 · as_of 2026-04-30T16:18:48Z\nhttps://github.com/Uniswap/v3-core/blob/d0831dc6b8a318df3872b6d68f6de135c9f3ec29/audits/tob/contracts/crytic/echidna/E2E_swap.sol#L386-L418\n\n```\nfunction test_swap_exactIn_oneForZero(uint128 _amount) public {\n        require(_amount != 0);\n```\n\n### uniswap-v3@3.0.0::test.UniswapV3Pool.swaps.spec::Decimal\n`uniswap-v3@3.0.0` · ⚠ version_defaulted · repo:d0831dc6b8a318df3872b6d68f6de135c9f3ec29 · as_of 2026-04-30T16:18:48Z\nhttps://github.com/Uniswap/v3-core/blob/d0831dc6b8a318df3872b6d68f6de135c9f3ec29/test/UniswapV3Pool.swaps.spec.ts#L1-L45\n\n```\nimport { Decimal } from 'decimal.js'\nimport { BigNumber, BigNumberish, ContractTransaction, Wallet } from 'ethers'\nimport { ethers, waffle } from 'hardhat'\n```\n\n### uniswap-v3@3.0.0::TestUniswapV3Router::swapForExact0Multi\n`uniswap-v3@3.0.0` · ⚠ version_defaulted · repo:d0831dc6b8a318df3872b6d68f6de135c9f3ec29 · as_of 2026-04-30T16:18:48Z\nhttps://github.com/Uniswap/v3-core/blob/d0831dc6b8a318df3872b6d68f6de135c9f3ec29/contracts/test/TestUniswapV3Router.sol#L12-L50\n\n```\nfunction swapForExact0Multi(\nfunction swapForExact1Multi(\nevent SwapCallback(int256 amount0Delta, int256 amount1Delta);\n(3 units in this chunk)\n```\n\n### uniswap-v3@3.0.0::TestUniswapV3Callee::__contract__\n`uniswap-v3@3.0.0` · ⚠ version_defaulted · repo:d0831dc6b8a318df3872b6d68f6de135c9f3ec29 · as_of 2026-04-30T16:18:48Z\nhttps://github.com/Uniswap/v3-core/blob/d0831dc6b8a318df3872b6d68f6de135c9f3ec29/contracts/test/TestUniswapV3Callee.sol#L15-L15\n\n```\ncontract TestUniswapV3Callee is IUniswapV3MintCallback, IUniswapV3SwapCallback, IUniswapV3FlashCallback\n```\n\n### uniswap-v3@3.0.0::TestUniswapV3SwapPay::__contract__\n`uniswap-v3@3.0.0` · ⚠ version_defaulted · repo:d0831dc6b8a318df3872b6d68f6de135c9f3ec29 · as_of 2026-04-30T16:18:48Z\nhttps://github.com/Uniswap/v3-core/blob/d0831dc6b8a318df3872b6d68f6de135c9f3ec29/contracts/test/TestUniswapV3SwapPay.sol#L9-L41\n\n```\ncontract TestUniswapV3SwapPay is IUniswapV3SwapCallback {\n    function swap(\n```"}],"structuredContent":{"intent":"integrate","recipe":{"project_id":"uniswap-v3","version":"70bc2e40","recipe_type":"exact-input-swap","last_validated":"2026-08-11","validated_by":"farseen (github: FarseenSh)","receipts":{"validated_on":"2026-08-11","validated_by":"farseen (github: FarseenSh)","checks":["attest","test","fork"],"chains_exercised":["ethereum","base","arbitrum"],"on_chain":"none recorded — this row exercises no chain, or its run broadcast nothing. A stated absence, never a gap: the receipt for such a row IS the suite result.","gas":"see `gas_notes` — the measured figures live there with their conditions, and a receipt that restated them without those conditions would be a number without its composition."},"body":"# Recipe: uniswap-v3 @3 :: exact-input-swap\n# STATUS: ✅ VALIDATED 2026-08-11 by farseen (github: FarseenSh) — 7 quotes · 9 structural · 7 fork assertions, and THE FLOW RAN ON ALL THREE CHAINS. (Banner and stamp changed in the SAME edit — see aave-v3, where this drifted twice.)\nproject_id: \"uniswap-v3\"    # ⚠ The locked P1 worklist brands the major into the id. §2 rules\n                            #   those ids are NOT renamed, and version_major is set redundantly.\nversion_major: 3            # the protocol major — and here it agrees with the id, unlike `dynamic`\nversion: \"70bc2e40\"         # ⚠ NOT a semver. SwapRouter02 publishes no version; this is the\n                            #   pinned commit's short SHA, the only version identity it has.\ntype: \"exact-input-swap\"\n\n# Every one of these had the FLOW run on it, not just the deployment inspected.\nchains: [ethereum, base, arbitrum]\n\n# ── THE DEPLOYMENTS ─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────\n# ⚠ SwapRouter02 is NOT at one address across chains. Verified on-chain by selector, not copied.#\n# ⚠ NAMED 2026-08-15 (F-4, protocol rule 9). Each chain previously mapped straight to a bare\n#   address, so the typed table produced a row with no contract name — \"(unnamed in recipe)\" —\n#   and the address could be served but not asked for. The name is NOT the author's: it is the\n#   contract name Sourcify reports for the verified source at that exact address on that exact\n#   chain, attested in sources.json. ⚠ NO ADDRESS CHANGED; only a name was added around it.\n# 🔴 THIS EDIT POSTDATES THE STAMP ABOVE and the stamp was not touched — this row needs a fresh\n#   curator run before launch. Every address here resolves to `SwapRouter02` on every chain listed.\ndeployments:\n  ethereum:\n    SwapRouter02: \"0x68b3465833fb72A70ecDF485E0e4C7bD8665Fc45\"\n  arbitrum:\n    SwapRouter02: \"0x68b3465833fb72A70ecDF485E0e4C7bD8665Fc45\"\n  base:\n    SwapRouter02: \"0x2626664c2603336E57B271c5C0b26F421741e481\"\n\n# ── WORKING EXAMPLE ─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────\n# Extracted VERBATIM to test/uniswap-v3/recipe/ and COMPILED BY FOUNDRY there, so \"the shipped\n# example is broken\" is a build failure rather than a discovery (recipe #1, D-1).\nworking_example:\n  source_protocol: \"uniswap-v3\"\n  source_url: \"https://github.com/Uniswap/swap-router-contracts/blob/70bc2e40dfca294c1cea9bf67a4036732ee54303/contracts/interfaces/IV3SwapRouter.sol\"\n  code: |\n    // ── WorkingExample.sol ──\n    // SPDX-License-Identifier: MIT\n    pragma solidity ^0.8.24;\n\n    interface IERC20 {\n        function approve(address spender, uint256 amount) external returns (bool);\n        function transferFrom(address from, address to, uint256 amount) external returns (bool);\n    }\n\n    /// SwapRouter02's V3 surface. SEVEN fields — there is no `deadline` here.\n    interface IV3SwapRouter {\n        struct ExactInputSingleParams {\n            address tokenIn;\n            address tokenOut;\n            uint24 fee;\n            address recipient;\n            uint256 amountIn;\n            uint256 amountOutMinimum;\n            uint160 sqrtPriceLimitX96;\n        }\n\n        function exactInputSingle(ExactInputSingleParams calldata params)\n            external\n            payable\n            returns (uint256 amountOut);\n    }\n\n    /// Where the deadline actually lives on SwapRouter02.\n    interface IMulticallExtended {\n        function multicall(uint256 deadline, bytes[] calldata data)\n            external\n            payable\n            returns (bytes[] memory results);\n    }\n\n    contract ExactInputSwapper {\n        address public immutable router;\n\n        /// ⚠ The router address is a CONSTRUCTOR ARGUMENT, deliberately. SwapRouter02 is at\n        ///   0x68b3465833fb72A70ecDF485E0e4C7bD8665Fc45 on Ethereum and Arbitrum but\n        ///   0x2626664c2603336E57B271c5C0b26F421741e481 on Base, so a hard-coded constant is a\n        ///   bug waiting for a deployment. See common_mistakes #3.\n        constructor(address router_) {\n            router = router_;\n        }\n\n        /// Swap an exact amount of tokenIn for as much tokenOut as possible.\n        ///\n        /// ⚠ THE DEADLINE IS NOT IN THE PARAMS. It is supplied by wrapping the call in\n        ///   multicall(deadline, …). Calling exactInputSingle directly compiles, runs, and has\n        ///   NO deadline protection whatsoever. See common_mistakes #2.\n        function swapExactInputSingle(\n            address tokenIn,\n            address tokenOut,\n            uint24 fee,\n            uint256 amountIn,\n            uint256 amountOutMinimum,\n            uint256 deadline\n        ) external returns (uint256 amountOut) {\n            IERC20(tokenIn).transferFrom(msg.sender, address(this), amountIn);\n            IERC20(tokenIn).approve(router, amountIn);\n\n            IV3SwapRouter.ExactInputSingleParams memory params = IV3SwapRouter.ExactInputSingleParams({\n                tokenIn: tokenIn,\n                tokenOut: tokenOut,\n                fee: fee,\n                recipient: msg.sender,\n                // ⚠ NEVER pass 0 here expecting a no-op. On SwapRouter02, 0 means \"swap the\n                //   router's entire balance of tokenIn\". See common_mistakes #4.\n                amountIn: amountIn,\n                amountOutMinimum: amountOutMinimum,\n                sqrtPriceLimitX96: 0\n            });\n\n            bytes[] memory calls = new bytes[](1);\n            calls[0] = abi.encodeCall(IV3SwapRouter.exactInputSingle, (params));\n\n            bytes[] memory results = IMulticallExtended(router).multicall(deadline, calls);","source_path":"recipes/uniswap-v3/exact-input-swap.yaml","requested_version":null,"exact_version_match":null,"body_truncated":true,"body_bytes":34282,"citations":["https://github.com/Uniswap/swap-router-contracts/blob/70bc2e40dfca294c1cea9bf67a4036732ee54303/contracts/interfaces/IV3SwapRouter.sol","https://github.com/Uniswap/v3-periphery/blob/0682387198a24c7cd63566a2c58398533860a5d1/contracts/interfaces/ISwapRouter.sol","https://github.com/Uniswap/swap-router-contracts/blob/70bc2e40dfca294c1cea9bf67a4036732ee54303/contracts/interfaces/IMulticallExtended.sol","https://github.com/Uniswap/universal-router","https://github.com/Uniswap/swap-router-contracts","https://raw.githubusercontent.com/Uniswap/swap-router-contracts/70bc2e40dfca294c1cea9bf67a4036732ee54303/contracts/interfaces/IV3SwapRouter.sol","https://github.com/Uniswap/swap-router-contracts/tree/70bc2e40dfca294c1cea9bf67a4036732ee54303","https://github.com/Uniswap/v3-periphery/tree/0682387198a24c7cd63566a2c58398533860a5d1"],"citations_capped":false,"body_cursor":"recipe:uniswap-v3@70bc2e40::exact-input-swap::body@5600","version_note":"⚠ Version disagreement: this recipe was validated against `uniswap-v3@70bc2e40`, while the units 